; apps/pim: mini-pim, a suite for organizing a life
; (docs/plans/plan_pim.md), in folders (folders only: one library,
; ix_pim):
;   mail/  the mail (docs/plans/plan_mail.md): its formats, Mail (a
;          message, RFC 5322), Mime (its parts, its encodings, its
;          charsets), Mail_thread (conversations, Zawinski's), the
;          author's playground's libs/networking/mail; its protocols,
;          Smtp and Imap (the clients), Smtp_server and Imap_server
;          (the servers' machines), and Lines, which carries them over
;          TCP or TLS; and Mail_item, a message as an item of the store
;   window/ Mail_window: the mail in a window, Gmail's keys, over the
;          store; Mail_sync (mail/) what it and the terminal's commands
;          do with the server, Conversations what they show
;   store/ the suite's store (docs/plans/plan_pim.md, ideas 1 and 3):
;          Item (lines of name: value, Mail's syntax, stamped) and
;          Items (a directory, a file an item, and the mail's cache)
; Pim.ml, the program: from a terminal (mini-pim send, list, read,
; archive, -offline), and with no command the window (window/);
; Maild.ml, mini-maild, the server its tests talk to
; (a file's text is the playground's: what it leaves unused stays, no
; warning of it an error)
(include_subdirs unqualified)

(library
 (name ix_pim)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules :standard \ Pim Maild)
 (flags (:standard -w -32-37-69))
 (libraries ix_playground ix_gui ix_graphics_software ix_tls ix_tcp ix_core
   caps unix))

; the program, with the platform that writes a frame to a file (the
; tests'); sdl/ is the one with a window, bin/mini-pim
(executable
 (name Pim)
 (modules Pim)
 (libraries ix_pim ix_playground ix_playground_render ix_playground_ppm ix_tls
   ix_tcp ix_core fpath caps unix))

(executable
 (name Maild)
 (public_name mini-maild)
 (package ix)
 (modules Maild)
 (libraries ix_pim ix_tls ix_tcp ix_core fpath caps unix))
